# What was actually measured

Backends          Groth16 (R1CS frontend, r1cs.NewBuilder) and PLONK (SCS frontend,
                  scs.NewBuilder), both over BN254
Curve             BN254. The scalar field is ~254 bits, so no INT8/INT32 quantity in any
                  task can overflow it; the A1 accumulator bound is checked against int64
                  in the reference computation, not against the field.
GPU               NOT measured. `WithIcicleAcceleration` is DEPRECATED in its own docstring
                  and round one of this benchmark is CPU-only by declaration.
PLONK SRS         test/unsafekzg, whose own docstring says "to be use for test purposes
                  only". This is NOT an MPC ceremony. Declared in RESULTS.md's conditions
                  line, not in a footnote.

